+# Parametric panel-count threshold — proposed prototype
+
+This task-local extension varies one episode-level rule parameter while leaving
+the approved production generator and canonical authority unchanged.
+
+| Parameter | Allowed value | Rule | Original/default |
+| --- | --- | --- | --- |
+| `min_panel_count` | `2` | output 1 when a panel has at least two color-6 cells | yes |
+| `min_panel_count` | `3` | output 1 when a panel has at least three color-6 cells | no |
+
+The setting is fixed across an episode. Inputs come from the selected generator's
+existing lawful 0/6/8 divider-grid grammar; every pair contains both count-2 and
+count-3 panels, so demonstrations distinguish the declared settings. The retained
+evidence uses three demonstrations and four distinct queries per setting. Exact
+Racket programs produce all retained labels and rival predictions; the adapter's
+Python labels are claims rechecked by the qualification worker.
+
+Run from the outer extracted packet directory:
+
+```sh
+python3 review.py run python3 \
+  generators/a9c4475d7cda/workspace/parametric/prototype.py \
+  --seed 2600 --demos 3 --queries 4 \
+  --out ../checks/parametric/panel-threshold-gallery
+
+python3 review.py run python3 -m pytest -q \
+  generators/a9c4475d7cda/tests/test_parametric_panel_threshold.py
+```
+
+Public challenge names are SHA-256 IDs of exact visible bytes. Public files contain
+only demonstration inputs/outputs and query inputs; settings, seeds, Racket source,
+and query answers remain private. `adapter.py` and `promotion.json` make the
+prototype ready for separate qualification, but do not approve it or admit data to
+training.
